-- COURAGE (18 verses)
('Joshua 1:9', 'This is my command — be strong and courageous! Do not be afraid or discouraged. For the LORD your God is with you wherever you go.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Deuteronomy 31:6', 'So be strong and courageous! Do not be afraid and do not panic before them. For the LORD your God will personally go ahead of you. He will neither fail you nor abandon you.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Isaiah 41:10', 'Don''t be afraid, for I am with you. Don''t be discouraged, for I am your God. I will strengthen you and help you. I will hold you up with my victorious right hand.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 27:14', 'Wait patiently for the LORD. Be brave and courageous. Yes, wait patiently for the LORD.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('2 Timothy 1:7', 'For God has not given us a spirit of fear and timidity, but of power, love, and self-discipline.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 56:3', 'But when I am afraid, I will put my trust in you.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Isaiah 43:1', 'But now, O Jacob, listen to the LORD who created you. O Israel, the one who formed you says, "Do not be afraid, for I have ransomed you. I have called you by name; you are mine."', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 118:6', 'The LORD is for me, so I will have no fear. What can mere people do to me?', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Romans 8:31', 'What shall we say about such wonderful things as these? If God is for us, who can ever be against us?', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('1 Chronicles 28:20', 'Then David continued, "Be strong and courageous, and do the work. Don''t be afraid or discouraged, for the LORD God, my God, is with you. He will not fail you or forsake you."', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 31:24', 'So be strong and courageous, all you who put your hope in the LORD!', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Proverbs 28:1', 'The wicked run away when no one is chasing them, but the godly are as bold as lions.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 112:7', 'They do not fear bad news; they confidently trust the LORD to care for them.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Isaiah 35:4', 'Say to those with fearful hearts, "Be strong, and do not fear, for your God is coming to destroy your enemies. He is coming to save you."', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Acts 4:31', 'After this prayer, the meeting place shook, and they were all filled with the Holy Spirit. Then they preached the word of God with boldness.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 23:4', 'Even when I walk through the darkest valley, I will not be afraid, for you are close beside me. Your rod and your staff protect and comfort me.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('John 14:27', 'I am leaving you with a gift — peace of mind and heart. And the peace I give is a gift the world cannot give. So don''t be troubled or afraid.', 'courage', 'NLT'),
('Hebrews 13:6', 'So we can say with confidence, "The LORD is my helper, so I will have no fear. What can mere people do to me?"', 'courage', 'NLT'),

-- PATIENCE (18 verses)
('James 1:2-4', 'Dear brothers and sisters, when troubles of any kind come your way, consider it an opportunity for great joy. For you know that when your faith is tested, your endurance has a chance to grow. So let it grow, for when your endurance is fully developed, you will be perfect and complete, needing nothing.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Romans 12:12', 'Rejoice in our confident hope. Be patient in trouble, and keep on praying.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Ecclesiastes 7:8', 'Finishing is better than starting. Patience is better than pride.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Galatians 6:9', 'So let''s not get tired of doing what is good. At just the right time we will reap a harvest of blessing if we don''t give up.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 37:7', 'Be still in the presence of the LORD, and wait patiently for him to act. Don''t worry about evil people who prosper or fret about their wicked schemes.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Hebrews 10:36', 'Patient endurance is what you need now, so that you will continue to do God''s will. Then you will receive all that he has promised.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Isaiah 40:31', 'But those who trust in the LORD will find new strength. They will soar high on wings like eagles. They will run and not grow weary. They will walk and not faint.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 40:1', 'I waited patiently for the LORD to help me, and he turned to me and heard my cry.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Romans 8:25', 'But if we look forward to something we don''t yet have, we must wait patiently and confidently.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Colossians 1:11', 'We also pray that you will be strengthened with all his glorious power so you will have all the endurance and patience you need. May you be filled with joy.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Proverbs 14:29', 'People with understanding control their anger; a hot temper shows great foolishness.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('2 Peter 3:9', 'The Lord isn''t really being slow about his promise, as some people think. No, he is being patient for your sake. He does not want anyone to be destroyed, but wants everyone to repent.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Lamentations 3:25', 'The LORD is good to those who depend on him, to those who search for him.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Proverbs 15:18', 'A hot-tempered person starts fights; a cool-tempered person stops them.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('1 Corinthians 13:4', 'Love is patient and kind. Love is not jealous or boastful or proud.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 27:14', 'Wait patiently for the LORD. Be brave and courageous. Yes, wait patiently for the LORD.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('Habakkuk 2:3', 'This vision is for a future time. It describes the end, and it will be fulfilled. If it seems slow in coming, wait patiently, for it will surely take place. It will not be delayed.', 'patience', 'NLT'),
('James 5:7-8', 'Dear brothers and sisters, be patient as you wait for the Lord''s return. Consider the farmers who patiently wait for the rains in the fall and in the spring. They eagerly look for the valuable harvest to ripen. You, too, must be patient. Take courage, for the coming of the Lord is near.', 'patience', 'NLT'),

-- JOY (18 verses)
('Nehemiah 8:10', 'And Nehemiah continued, "Go and celebrate with a feast of rich foods and sweet drinks, and share gifts of food with people who have nothing prepared. This is a sacred day before our Lord. Don''t be dejected and sad, for the joy of the LORD is your strength!"', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 16:11', 'You will show me the way of life, granting me the joy of your presence and the pleasures of living with you forever.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('John 15:11', 'I have told you these things so that you will be filled with my joy. Yes, your joy will overflow!', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 30:5', 'For his anger lasts only a moment, but his favor lasts a lifetime! Weeping may last through the night, but joy comes with the morning.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Romans 15:13', 'I pray that God, the source of hope, will fill you completely with joy and peace because you trust in him. Then you will overflow with confident hope through the power of the Holy Spirit.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Philippians 4:4', 'Always be full of joy in the Lord. I say it again — rejoice!', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('James 1:2', 'Dear brothers and sisters, when troubles of any kind come your way, consider it an opportunity for great joy.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 126:5', 'Those who plant in tears will harvest with shouts of joy.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 5:11', 'But let all who take refuge in you rejoice; let them sing joyful praises forever. Spread your protection over them, that all who love your name may be filled with joy.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Isaiah 61:10', 'I am overwhelmed with joy in the LORD my God! For he has dressed me with the clothing of salvation and draped me in a robe of righteousness.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('1 Peter 1:8', 'You love him even though you have never seen him. Though you do not see him now, you trust him; and you rejoice with a glorious, inexpressible joy.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 98:4', 'Shout to the LORD, all the earth; break out in praise and sing for joy!', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 47:1', 'Come, everyone! Clap your hands! Shout to God with joyful praise!', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Psalm 118:24', 'This is the day the LORD has made. We will rejoice and be glad in it.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Habakkuk 3:18', 'Yet I will rejoice in the LORD! I will be joyful in the God of my salvation!', 'joy', 'NLT'),
('Zephaniah 3:17', 'For the LORD your God is living among you. He is a mighty savior. He will take delight in you with gladness. With his love, he will calm all your fears. He will rejoice over you with joyful songs.', 'joy', 'NLT'),
